sdmsg (1.0.0) unstable; urgency=medium

  * GUI: launch without target; menubar/toolbar/statusbar; device
    picker.
  * Prefer udisks/FUSE for image SHA-1 mounts; fakeroot cannot grant
    real mount caps.
  * GUI: -g short option; Start before Pause (re-enable after stop);
    Edit menu (On raw disk / On Files / Preferences).
  * Use wxStatusBar with a work-state icon. Log view is a filterable
    table (icon, time, level, message).
  * Restore Start/Pause/Stop toolbar buttons. Status leaves "Starting"
    when the run advances or fails, and the scan grid stays visible.
  * Remember the last opened file, device, and database and reopen them
    on the next GUI launch.
  * Add a GUI end-to-end test that drives a throwaway file.
  * SHA-1 of a regular file or loop device mounts read-only with FUSE
    and no longer asks.
  * GUI never prompts on the terminal. SHA-1 runs only when a database
    is enabled. Log level lives in the View menu. Close clears the
    grid. Edit has Dry-run (read-only scan). Restart repaints the grid.
  * Database Open can create a new file. File Browser uses the current
    target (FUSE/udisks mount). Sync adds SHA-1 for new files, drops
    dangling rows, and asks on conflicts. MIME icons; Open / Open as.
  * Toolbar: Drive / Manifest / Start / Pause / Stop / Browser / About.
    Drive and Manifest are sticky toggles. File and Database menus match.
    View Logging level submenu (Error..Trace). Conflict dialog can apply
    to the rest and remember.
  * Browser mounts the current Drive (FUSE/udisks, partition offset when
    needed) before showing files.
  * Edit: Write through (O_DIRECT/fdatasync). Without it, grid cells stay
    blue until flushed (cachestat / sync_file_range) then green. Verify
    writes re-reads via O_DIRECT (never page-cache compare).
  * GUI logs also go to stdout. SHA-1 FUSE mounts detect the filesystem
    first (ext4 no longer falls through to ntfs-3g in the error text).
  * Without Write through, do not force per-block writeback (was making
    cache path as slow as sync). Rewrite end logs stats; one fdatasync
    then Cached→Ok. FUSE EPERM explains missing setuid fusermount.
  * Status bar: icons on phase/pct/rate/eta/cells/db fields. Clarify
    fuse2fs -o fakeroot cannot grant mount privilege.
  * When host FUSE mount fails with EPERM, enter a user+mount namespace
    and retry (fuse2fs/ntfs-3g work without setuid fusermount).
  * Enter user mount namespace at process start (before threads) so GUI
    FUSE works. Without Write through, do not fdatasync after rewrite
    (keeps cache speed; cells stay blue until flushed).
  * Rewrite: drop per-block cachestat (O(n^2) snail). Browser list shows
    SHA-1; skip virtual MIME icon paths that are not real files.
  * Edit write-cache mode (radio): Write through / cachestat (default) /
    mincore; flush probe every 0.78s.
  * After rewrite, keep flushing/polling until Cached cells turn green.
    Browser: do not list root DB under unknown folders (lost+found).
  * After rewrite (~1s without Write through), full-disk sync runs on a
    background thread; the worker keeps polling/heartbeat until sync ends,
    then all cells turn green without re-query (avoids UI freeze on sync).
  * Preferences: SHA-1 days, block size, write-cache mode, flush poll
    interval, verify writes, dry-run, run mode.
  * Prefer already-mounted device-root manifest.db unless -d was given.
    Database → DB Admin launches sqlitebrowser. Menu items use icons.
    Suggests: sqlitebrowser.
  * Enter user+mount namespace before threads so Browse can FUSE-mount when
    host fusermount returns EPERM. Manifest menu: Create default / Use
    external SQLite / Close / User mounts / Validate / Browse / SQLite admin.
    alert_box mirrors dialogs to stderr.
  * Validate: rebuild file paths for extent orphan check (no file.path);
    subtitle wraps with dialog width. Quiet AT-SPI dbind warnings in GUI.
  * Validate dialog: re-run via bottom-left Validate. User mounts buttons
    pin to dialog bottom. Host privilege agent (before userns) so Apply /
    Turn off work despite sudo audit plugin. Files status: scanned
    files/bytes, record count, field icons, work indicator.
  * Files browser View menu: hidden files, thumbnails, arrange, zoom,
    Icon/List/Compact (menu + top-right switchers); Ctrl+wheel zooms.
  * File/toolbar: Eject and Safely Remove (both close the drive; close
    in-drive manifest first). Close also closes a manifest on the drive.
  * GUI privileges: pkexec only (no sudo); stable script path; run Apply
    off the UI thread with wxYield so the polkit dialog stays usable.
    Drop User mounts from the main toolbar. Browser: icon-only view
    switchers (3×3 grid), row-major icon view, XPM thumbs, refresh keeps
    selection, safer tree keyboard navigation.
  * Warn before switching Raw → Files mode. Persist browser view options
    and Preferences under ~/.config/sdtouch/ (auto-rewrite window
    default 6 months).

 -- Lenik (谢继雷) <lenik@bodz.net>  Wed, 23 Sep 2026 23:35:00 +0800

sdmsg (0.1.0) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Rewrite as SD card data massage tool (wxWidgets, linear/recursive,
    SQLite).
  * C++/wxWidgets UI with progress grid, pause, speed/ETA, badblocks
    export.
  * Linear and recursive modes; FAT/exFAT, NTFS, ext2/3/4 on-disk
    walkers.
  * SQLite tracking of paths, SHA-1, massage/verify counts and bad
    extents.
  * Auto-unmount/remount (-m); headless default with optional --gui.
  * Rewrite allocated FS data only; SHA-1 after mount; NTFS raw attrs.
  * Add make-testbases/run-testdrive scripts and fixture README for FS
    image tests.
  * Fix FAT/exFAT directory chain walks so recursive mode covers all
    files.
  * Strengthen testdrive: content integrity, refuse-when-mounted; lint
    cleanups.

